{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["These are the words — according to its plain sense: all the items mentioned in this verse are places, as we find that Scripture is accustomed to giving sign within sign for the places it wishes to specify where. לך לך: מקדם לבית אל ויט אהלה בית אל מים והעי מקדם. In the section of בשלח: וישובו ויחנו לפני פי החירות בין מגדול ובין הים לפני בעל צפון. In the book of Judges: הנה חג לה' בשילה מימים ימימה אשר מצפונה לבית אל מזרחה השמש למסלה העלה מבית אל שכמה ומנגב ללבונה. How much more so does one need to specify where the commandments were spoken, as written: וידבר ה' אל משה בהר סיני. In the land of Egypt: החדש הזה. וידבר ה' אל משה בהר סיני. בערבות מואב. So too here he makes sign within sign, and so he says and repeats this matter when Moshe comes to set forth the commandments: אלה העדות והחקים והמשפטים אשר דבר משה וגו׳. בעבר הירדן בגיא מול בית פעור בארץ סיחון מלך האמורי הואיל משה וגו׳." "Beyond the Jordan — and on which side of the Jordan?" "In the wilderness — on that side of the Jordan which is toward the wilderness where Israel was forty years, which is called 'beyond the Jordan' by those dwelling in the land of Israel, and not the side of the Jordan that is toward the land of Israel — for that too is called 'beyond the Jordan' by those journeying through the wilderness where Israel was." "In the Arabah — that is, in what place in the wilderness? In that wilderness which is in the plains of Moab." "Opposite Suph — the Sea of Suph begins from the east of the land of Israel, as stated: ושתי את גבלך מים סוף עד ים פלשתים וגו׳ — that is, from east to west; and it is the Dead Sea, which is written in the border description as the southeastern corner in אלה מסעי, and also in the section of ואתחנן — וכל הערבה עבר הירדן מזרחה ועד ים הערבה — and this is the Sea of Suph that is by the plains of Moab." "Between Paran and between Tofel — like: between Bet El and between HaAi." "And Lavan and Hatzerot and Di Zahav — all are place-names by the plain sense." "And Di Zahav — like: Bat Mi Zahav, which is a proper name in its plain sense."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The bracketed editorial heading [בפרשת בשלח] is rendered as Rashbam's own words, following the Hebrew as given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:38:23.783939851Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}